running|activity|NOUN|fast movement on foot|The activity of moving quickly on foot, especially for exercise or as a sport.|chạy bộ|He took up running after joining a local sports club.|Anh ấy tham gia câu lạc bộ thể thao ở địa phương rồi bắt đầu tập chạy bộ.|Uncountable; go running or take up running. This record proposes the activity noun.|running
crude|unrefined|ADJECTIVE|not refined|Still in a natural state and not yet processed or purified.|thô, chưa tinh chế|The pipeline carries crude oil to the refinery.|Đường ống dẫn dầu thô đến nhà máy lọc dầu.|Usually before a material noun, especially crude oil.|crude
crude|offensive|ADJECTIVE|offensively rude|Rude or vulgar in a way that causes offence.|thô tục|A crude comment spoiled the friendly atmosphere.|Một lời nhận xét thô tục làm hỏng bầu không khí thân thiện.|Often describes jokes, remarks or language; expresses disapproval.|crude
crude|roughly-made|ADJECTIVE|rough and simple|Made or worked out in a simple way without much care, precision or detail.|thô sơ, sơ sài|She drew a crude map to show where the footpath began.|Cô ấy vẽ một bản đồ sơ sài để chỉ nơi đường mòn bắt đầu.|Can describe objects, methods or estimates; something crude may still be useful.|crude
unsettle|worry|VERB|make uneasy|To make someone feel anxious, worried or less confident.|làm bất an, khiến không yên tâm|The unexplained noise unsettled the guests.|Tiếng động không rõ nguyên nhân khiến các vị khách bất an.|Transitive; unsettle someone. Often used with events or information as the subject.|unsettle
offspring|children|NOUN|children or young|The children of a person or the young produced by an animal.|con, con cái|The fox moved her offspring to a quieter den.|Con cáo mẹ chuyển các con của nó đến một hang yên tĩnh hơn.|The singular and plural form is offspring; do not add an s.|offspring
dear|beloved|ADJECTIVE|loved and valued|Loved or valued deeply by someone.|thân yêu, yêu quý|She smiled when she heard her dear friend's voice.|Cô ấy mỉm cười khi nghe giọng người bạn thân yêu.|Can occur before a noun or in dear to someone.|dear
dear|dismay|INTERJECTION|mild dismay|Used in expressions of surprise, worry or disappointment.|ôi trời, ôi chao|Oh dear, the biscuits are burnt.|Ôi trời, bánh quy bị cháy rồi.|Usually in oh dear or dear me; this is an exclamation rather than an adjective.|dear
prescription|medicine-order|NOUN|authorized medicine instruction|An instruction from an authorized health professional allowing a patient to obtain specified medicine.|đơn thuốc|The pharmacist read the dosage written on the prescription.|Dược sĩ đọc liều dùng được ghi trên đơn thuốc.|Countable; a prescription for a medicine. Who may prescribe depends on the local system.|prescription
leadership|leading-ability|NOUN|guiding others|The action or ability of guiding and organizing other people.|sự lãnh đạo, khả năng lãnh đạo|The rescue team benefited from her steady leadership.|Đội cứu hộ được hỗ trợ bởi sự lãnh đạo vững vàng của cô ấy.|Usually uncountable in this sense; leadership of a team or under someone's leadership.|leadership
heat|hotness|NOUN|hotness or thermal energy|High temperature, or the energy that makes something hot.|nhiệt, sức nóng|The bricks retained heat long after the fire went out.|Những viên gạch giữ nhiệt rất lâu sau khi lửa tắt.|Usually uncountable; heat from a source or the heat of a place.|heat
heat|make-hot|VERB|make hotter|To raise the temperature of something.|làm nóng, đun nóng|He heated the milk in a small saucepan.|Anh ấy đun nóng sữa trong một chiếc nồi nhỏ.|Transitive here; heat something or heat it up.|heat
touch|make-contact|VERB|make physical contact|To put a hand or another part of the body against something.|chạm vào|The toddler reached out to touch the smooth stone.|Đứa trẻ mới biết đi đưa tay ra chạm vào viên đá nhẵn.|Transitive; touch something directly, without to before the object.|touch
touch|brief-contact|NOUN|brief physical contact|A brief act of putting a hand or other body part against someone or something.|cái chạm, sự chạm nhẹ|A gentle touch on her arm brought her back to the conversation.|Một cái chạm nhẹ vào cánh tay khiến cô ấy chú ý trở lại cuộc trò chuyện.|Countable; a touch on a part of the body.|touch
picture|photograph|NOUN|photographic image|An image produced by a camera.|bức ảnh|The guide took a picture of our group beside the lighthouse.|Hướng dẫn viên chụp ảnh nhóm chúng tôi bên ngọn hải đăng.|Countable; take a picture of someone or something.|picture
picture|drawn-image|NOUN|drawn or painted image|An image made by drawing or painting.|bức tranh, hình vẽ|Her picture of the garden used only green and yellow paint.|Bức tranh khu vườn của cô ấy chỉ dùng sơn xanh lá và vàng.|Countable; draw or paint a picture of something.|picture
picture|imagine|VERB|form a mental image|To imagine someone, something or a situation in your mind.|hình dung, tưởng tượng|I could picture him sitting at that enormous desk.|Tôi có thể hình dung anh ấy đang ngồi bên chiếc bàn khổng lồ đó.|Transitive; picture someone doing something, without to before doing.|picture
table|furniture|NOUN|flat-topped furniture|A piece of furniture with a raised flat surface for working, eating or placing things on.|bàn|The round table fits neatly into the corner of the kitchen.|Chiếc bàn tròn vừa vặn gọn gàng trong góc bếp.|Countable; at the table for eating or working, on the table for objects.|table
table|data-grid|NOUN|rows and columns of data|Information arranged in rows and columns to make comparisons easier.|bảng số liệu|The table compares rainfall in six mountain villages.|Bảng số liệu so sánh lượng mưa ở sáu làng miền núi.|Countable; a table of figures. A table need not be drawn on paper.|table
duration|length-of-time|NOUN|length of time|The amount of time for which an event or activity lasts.|thời lượng, khoảng thời gian kéo dài|The duration of the performance was ninety minutes.|Thời lượng của buổi biểu diễn là chín mươi phút.|Duration of something; for the duration means throughout that period.|duration
intelligence|mental-ability|NOUN|ability to understand|The ability to learn, understand and reason about things.|trí thông minh, trí tuệ|The puzzle called for intelligence as well as patience.|Câu đố đòi hỏi trí thông minh lẫn sự kiên nhẫn.|Usually uncountable; descriptions of intelligence do not by themselves establish a formal test score.|intelligence
intelligence|strategic-information|NOUN|information about threats|Information gathered about an opponent or possible threat, especially for military or security purposes.|tin tình báo|The officers compared intelligence from several sources.|Các sĩ quan đối chiếu tin tình báo từ nhiều nguồn.|Uncountable; gather intelligence or intelligence about a threat.|intelligence
collaboration|working-together|NOUN|joint work|Working together with other people or organizations to create something or reach a goal.|sự hợp tác|The mural grew out of a collaboration between students and local painters.|Bức tranh tường ra đời từ sự hợp tác giữa học sinh và các họa sĩ địa phương.|Uncountable for joint work; countable for a particular collaborative project.|collaboration
dedication|commitment|NOUN|committed effort|Continued effort and commitment to something considered important.|sự tận tâm, cống hiến|His dedication to restoring the park inspired new volunteers.|Sự tận tâm của anh ấy với việc khôi phục công viên truyền cảm hứng cho các tình nguyện viên mới.|Uncountable; dedication to a task or to doing something.|dedication
artery|blood-vessel|NOUN|vessel carrying blood away|A blood vessel that carries blood away from the heart.|động mạch|The model uses red tubes to represent the body's arteries.|Mô hình dùng các ống màu đỏ để biểu thị các động mạch của cơ thể.|Countable; plural arteries. Direction of flow defines arteries, not the oxygen level of the blood.|artery
exotic|foreign-unfamiliar|ADJECTIVE|unfamiliar from afar|Unusual or unfamiliar to someone because it comes from a distant place.|lạ, ngoại lai|The gardener tried growing exotic fruit in a heated greenhouse.|Người làm vườn thử trồng loại quả ngoại lai trong một nhà kính được sưởi ấm.|What seems exotic depends on the observer and context; avoid using it as a label for people.|exotic
queue|waiting-line|NOUN|line of waiting people|A line of people waiting their turn for something.|hàng chờ, hàng người xếp chờ|The queue for the museum stretched around the corner.|Hàng người chờ vào bảo tàng kéo dài qua góc phố.|Countable; join a queue or a queue for something. Especially common in British English.|queue
queue|wait-in-line|VERB|wait in a line|To stand in a line with other people while waiting your turn.|xếp hàng chờ|We queued for tickets despite the rain.|Chúng tôi xếp hàng chờ mua vé mặc trời mưa.|Intransitive; queue for something or queue at a place. Especially common in British English.|queue
insist|demand-firmly|VERB|demand firmly|To say firmly that something must happen or be done.|khăng khăng yêu cầu|The coach insisted on checking every player's equipment.|Huấn luyện viên khăng khăng đòi kiểm tra trang bị của từng cầu thủ.|Insist on doing something or insist that something should happen; not insist to do.|insist
deck|ship-floor|NOUN|floor on a ship|A floor or open platform on a ship.|boong tàu|The crew secured the ropes on the lower deck.|Thủy thủ đoàn buộc chặt các dây thừng trên boong dưới.|Countable; on deck can omit the article when referring generally to the ship's deck.|deck
deck|outdoor-platform|NOUN|outdoor floor|An outdoor floor or platform next to a house, often built from wood.|sàn ngoài trời|They placed two chairs on the deck overlooking the pond.|Họ đặt hai ghế trên sàn ngoài trời nhìn ra ao.|Countable; often a wooden deck, though other materials are possible.|deck
deck|playing-cards|NOUN|set of playing cards|A complete set of cards used for playing a card game.|bộ bài|One card was missing from the deck, so we used another set.|Bộ bài bị thiếu một lá nên chúng tôi dùng bộ khác.|Countable; a deck of cards. The number of cards depends on the game.|deck
